== the fault vocabulary, digits normalised ==
   a \u escape with a non-hex digit
   a high surrogate with no low surrogate
   a js result carries no call id
   a low surrogate with no high surrogate
   a message must be a JSON object
   a message sequence must be a whole number
   a message sequence must not be negative
   a message with no "t"
   a number too large for this protocol
   a number with a leading zero
   a number with no digits
   a range carries no region id
   a range must be two non-negative numbers
   a raw control byte inside a string
   a string longer than # bytes
   a string was never closed
   a value cannot start with byte #
   ack carries no batch number
   an array longer than #
   an event carries no handler id
   an event payload must be an object
   an object key must be a string
   an object with more than # members
   an unknown string escape
   attach carries no circuit id
   expected , or ] in an array
   expected , or } in an object
   expected : after an object key
   expected null
   expected true
   nav carries no url
   nesting deeper than #
   resume carries no acknowledged batch
   resume carries no circuit id
   the message ended early
   the message is # bytes, over the #-byte limit
   this protocol carries integers only
   trailing bytes after the message
   unknown event name
   unknown message kind
   (40 distinct)

